  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Performance\n\n- Method setups no longer allocate queues or take a lock (#438, closes #405). Each method setup used to create two ConcurrentQueues, and each Then() step another. Until the steps ran out, every call also took a lock to advance them. Steps now live in a lock-free ReturnValueSequence, and callbacks in a list created on the first Callback. Indexer getter return values use the same sequence, as property getters already did. Per setup:\n\n  | Setup | 1.0.7 | 1.0.8 |\n  | --- | ---: | ---: |\n  | Returns(4) | 1,949 B | 389 B |\n  | Returns(1).Then().Returns(2).Then().Returns(3) | 3,864 B | 720 B |\n  | Throws(exception) | 2,032 B | 472 B |\n  | Returns(4).Callback(...) | 1,944 B | 440 B |\n  | indexer Getter().Returns(5) | 1,208 B | 480 B |\n\n  A call that runs a callback now allocates 96 B instead of 168 B, the same as a call without one.\n- Generic methods skip type adaptation when the type arguments already match (#433, closes #401). Verification no longer converts the criteria once per recorded call, so verifying against 1,000 recorded calls costs the same as against one. A matched Echo<string> call with two setups allocates at most 120 B, down from 216 B.\n- Edits rebuild less of each target's model (#436, closes #403). On every edit, the generator rebuilt or recompared several parts of each registered target's model. An edit with 20 registered targets now allocates about 25% less in the generator, for example 4.0 MB instead of 5.4 MB. The generated code is unchanged.",
